  "body": "## What changed\n\nAn area round a part (`StartSide::around_part`, the 2D Offset Outside band) now has one ring set for each start side. The rings are the offsets of the part, clipped to the cutter-centre area. Decision: `docs/decisions/3744-one-ring-set.md`.\n\n- Inside walks the set from the part out (the old Inside order).\n- Outside walks the same pieces mirrored (`ring_side::mirror`). Each piece runs the other way, so climb stays climb. The outer edge is the first ring and the part wall is the last ring.\n- Auto selects one side in one place (`ring_side::resolve`). Auto is Outside when the stock footprint is known and the outer edge stays in air, else Inside. The resolved side drives the rings, the links and the entry. `generate.rs` sends the stock footprint for Auto round a part.\n- Round a part, the #3567 dead-end ramp marks stop (issue step 6). Pockets keep them; #3748 retires them.\n- `ring_side::share_ends` snaps a ring end onto the boundary walk within 0.1 um, the closing chord included. A ring end 3 nm off its chord gave a crossing on the block of `shoulder_adaptive`.\n- #3788 (c): `order()` judges a full-width cut by the flanks law of the meter (`level_flanks`). Each full-width cut is named on the path.\n- #3788 (a): fill rings (`ring_fill`). Where the rings of two sides of the part merge, a band gets the same distance curve at half (and a quarter) of a step. A fill is a level curve of the same distance, so it crosses no ring, and Inside and Outside walk the same fills.\n- Not changed: pockets, the 3-D levels (their levels are only renumbered), the Adaptive plan, the entry (#3746) and the links (#3747).\n\n## Readings\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| Dog bone: Outside floor runs that end on the part wall (the last run excluded) | 13 of 14 | 0 |\n| Dog bone: Inside and Outside ring sets | 30 and 22 pieces, different | equal |\n| Auto | `waterline_passes` | the path of Outside (stock known) or Inside (no stock) |\n| fig8 Outside: full-width meter points | 0 (stock-parallel rings); 495 (one set, without fills) | 21 (single samples at 7 ring corners on 3 levels), named |\n| fig8 Inside: full-width meter points | 10686, waist cuts not named | 10662, each named (wall note and narrow note) |\n| fig8 crossings, Inside and Outside | not read | 0 |\n\n## Pins\n\n- `machining2d::ring_side::tests::inside_and_outside_cut_the_same_rings` (red first)\n- `machining2d::ring_side::tests::auto_picks_one_side_of_the_one_ring_set` (red first)\n- `machining2d::ring_side::tests::the_mirror_reverses_each_piece_and_swaps_the_ends_of_the_order`\n- `machining2d::ring_side::tests::a_ring_end_off_the_boundary_chord_by_nanometres_is_shared`\n- `machining2d::level_flanks::tests::the_flanks_law_reads_a_slot_and_passes_a_side_cut`\n- `machining2d::ring_fill::tests::a_band_with_a_ring_gap_gets_a_fill_and_a_whole_band_none`\n- `pass_start_levels::one_ring_set::outside_rings_follow_the_part` (red first: 14 of 14)\n- `pass_start_levels::one_ring_set::auto_is_inside_or_outside` (red first)\n- `pass_start_levels::one_ring_set::the_one_ring_set_posts_no_crossing_feeds`\n- `offset_pass_start::fig8_start_sides_have_no_crossing` (heavy; not shown red first)\n- `offset_pass_start::fig8_inside_offset_names_each_full_width_cut` (heavy)\n\n## Pins whose reading moved\n\n- `offset_pass_start::fig8_auto_offset_keeps_every_lateral_rapid_at_the_clearance_plane`: Auto is Outside on fig8, so each level starts outside the stock box. The issue asks for this.\n- `offset_pass_start::fig8_outside_offset_cuts_no_move_at_full_width` (heavy): 0 -> at most 21 points, each named by the narrow note, and no wall note. The 21 are single samples at 7 ring corners. #3788 stays open for them. The pin goes back to 0 when they are fixed.\n\n## Gates (head `6be6b1265`)\n\n- `camcraft-motion --lib` (machining2d, machining3d): 294 passed.\n- `camcraft-motion`: `pass_start_levels`, `pass_start_engagement`, `pocket3d_pass_start`, `avoid_adaptive`, `top_z_stock_over`, `circular_ring_links`, `bore_pass_start`, `finish3d_pass_start`: green.\n- `camcraft-app` (debug): `offset_pass_start`, `pocket_pass_start`, `pocket3d_pass_start`, `adaptive_pass_start`, `shoulder_adaptive`, `flute_reach`, `strategy_fallback`: green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Targeted heavy step `app heavy: offset_pass_start`: 4 passed.\n- The full quick gate ran green on `ef3372b11`, the head before the review. It did not run again on this head.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full quick gate on this head, the other heavy lanes, and the light lane.\n- The private model of #3741.\n\nChangelog: 2D Offset \"Pass starts at\" round a part: Auto, Inside and Outside now cut the same contour-parallel rings (offsets of the part), with fill rings where two sides of the part merge. The choice changes only the start side and the ring order, and Auto selects Inside or Outside. Outside rings no longer stop on the part wall, and each cut of the full tool width is named on the path.\n\nEffort: max (no escalation).\n\nRefs #3788\n\nFixes #3744\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
